===
matches
Returns true if the regular expression pattern matches the entire string.

matches(pattern, s)

matches("[0-9]+", "123")      # true
matches("[0-9]+", "abc123")   # false
===
find
Returns the first substring matching the pattern.
Returns [@error, :not_found] if no match.

find(pattern, s)

find("[0-9]+", "abc123def")    # "123"
find("[0-9]+", "abcdef")       # [@error, :not_found]
===
find_all
Returns a list of all substrings matching the pattern.

find_all(pattern, s)

find_all("[0-9]+", "a1b2c3")    # ["1", "2", "3"]
===
replace
Replaces all occurrences of the pattern with the replacement string.

replace(pattern, s, repl)

replace("[0-9]", "a1b2c3", "X")    # "aXbXcX"
===
replace_first
Replaces only the first occurrence of the pattern.

replace_first(pattern, s, repl)

replace_first("[0-9]", "a1b2c3", "X")    # "aXb2c3"
===
split
Splits the string by the pattern and returns a list of parts.

split(pattern, s)

split(",\\s*", "a, b, c")    # ["a", "b", "c"]
